From 2a94921185dc405bda6be830e74172aac6d0bf69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 23:06:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] securize: rework to property-based toggle with GSI
 fingerprint tracking

remove stale property overrides from rw-system.sh and base.mk, replace
with post-boot spoofing in phh-on-boot.sh that hides build props from
root detection. add property handler for persist.sys.phh.securize so
the toggle survives factory resets. gate the anti-detection spoofing on
/metadata/securize_disable.

also track GSI fingerprint changes across upgrades so
PackageManagerService detects upgrades correctly.

remove persist.sys.usb.config=adb default from base.mk -- adb is
disabled by default on release builds; enabling it requires the usual
developer options + usb debugging toggle. debug builds re-enable it
via the debug tier.

replace old persist.sys.phh.adb_secure=1 handler with property
trigger that uses magisk SELinux context to hide oem_unlock_allowed
from root detection.

note: adbd status hiding removed -- spoofing init.svc.adbd caused init
segfaults on samsung exynos devices when usb config changed. release
builds already disable adb by default; users who enable debugging can
hide it via magisk modules instead.

verified: all release-builds patches apply cleanly
